Add companion identifier APIs to ontology-term-resolution (#262)

* Add companion identifier APIs to ontology-term-resolution.

OLS stays the emit/validate authority. Prefix shape, landing pages, and lab shorthand now have scripts so agents do not invent CURIEs or call ZOOMA unfiltered.

Co-authored-by: Cursor &lt;cursoragent@cursor.com&gt;

* Emit only resolvable landing-page URLs from Bioregistry mappings.

preferred_prefix is not the Identifiers.org namespace, so templating it
printed dead ORPHA/OBA links next to the rejection note.

Co-authored-by: Cursor &lt;cursoragent@cursor.com&gt;

---------

Co-authored-by: Cursor &lt;cursoragent@cursor.com&gt;

Revert &quot;chore: post-merge follow-ups for #252&quot;

This reverts commit c23b718. The squash merge of #252 was refused by
GitHub on a README conflict, so the skill never landed and the README
and collection version were bumped for a skill that is not in the tree.
Back to 165 skills / 2.68.0 until #252 is rebased and merged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 &lt;noreply@anthropic.com&gt;

Add companion literature APIs to paper-lookup (#263)

Document OpenCitations, PubTator3, Zenodo, Figshare, ROR, BioStudies, and DOAJ so agents route repository, affiliation, entity, and journal-OA questions without treating HTTP 200 as success.

Co-authored-by: Cursor &lt;cursoragent@cursor.com&gt;
